  "conventions": [
    "Sources inspected on 2026-11-13; no project reference labels or lexicon used.",
    "Support the published onset and final inventory, including 2018 a/oet, plus standalone syllabic m/ng. This is structural conversion, not lexical or acoustic validation.",
    "Canonical z/c are single tied affricates t͡s/t͡sʰ; preserve aspiration, labialization, syllabicity, vowel length and unreleased stop codas.",
    "Use PyCantonese vowel qualities and rounded offglides; restore vowel length from the scheme. PyCantonese sourceIPA preserves its original length-unspecified notation separately.",
    "Canonical i/u become ɪ/ʊ before ng/k. Alternative scheme transcriptions remain component variants, not predictions or exhaustive combinations.",
    "A rime's configured phones are nucleus then coda, including vowel offglides. Affricates and labialized stops each occupy one phone; no IPA string is split by Unicode characters.",
    "Bare eo/y, nonstandard onsets, onset-bearing syllabic nasals, and unlisted finals remain unsupported; yu represents the front rounded vowel yː.",
    "Missing tone is unknown. Only ASCII tone numbers 1-6 are supported. Structural conversion does not reject checked syllables with changed tones: Rime Cantonese attests hap2, dip2 and aap2. Mapping is not lexical or acoustic validation."
  ],
